# ============================================================
# Migration & parity tooling ONLY — never installed in the image
# ============================================================
# The Postgres driver the backfill, parity and one-off analysis scripts under
# `scripts/` need to read the frozen Postgres backup. Split out of
# `requirements.in` on 2026-08-18 at teardown, when `app/db/connection.py`
# moved to `scripts/migration/pg_connection.py` and `app/` stopped importing
# psycopg entirely.
#
# `tests/unit/test_app_image_has_no_pg_driver.py` fails if psycopg comes back
# into `requirements.in`, or if any module under `app/` imports it.
#
# Install locally with:
#   pip install -r requirements-migration.in

psycopg[binary,pool]==3.2.6

# psycopg2 as well as psycopg3, and they are DIFFERENT PACKAGES. Four retained
# tools import the v2 API — `pg_embeddings_to_mongo`, `db_audit`,
# `build_migration_ledger` and `.claude/hooks/_check_idle_txn` — while the
# archive pool and the parity instruments use v3.
#
# Pinned here on 2026-08-30. Until then it was in NO requirements file at all,
# installed by hand into trading-service/.venv and into the system python, and
# that gap was load-bearing in the wrong direction: `_check_cycle_running.py`
# asserted in prose that psycopg2 "is not installed", which was true of the
# IMAGE and false of the box — and the false half is what let eight silent
# readers keep answering from the frozen archive.
#
# Not uninstalled, deliberately. ch.106 proposed removing it to make the
# remaining readers loud; the readers are ported now and `DATABASE_URL` is out
# of `.env` (5f6410f), so they are loud already, and uninstalling would take the
# retained archive tooling with it. Same rule as psycopg3: migration tooling,
# never `requirements.in`, or it lands in the image and
# tests/unit/test_app_image_has_no_pg_driver.py fails the build.
psycopg2-binary==2.9.12

# The SQL parser `scripts/sql_to_mongo.py` translates through, and therefore
# what `scripts/codemod_pg_to_mongo.py` needs to run. Pinned here on
# 2026-08-19 because it was in NO requirements file at all — installed by hand
# into trading-service/.venv and nowhere else, so the codemod simply did not
# run in a fresh checkout or in trading-client, and the only symptom was an
# ImportError at the moment someone tried to use it.
#
# Migration tooling, not runtime: nothing under `app/` imports it, and it must
# stay out of `requirements.in` for the same reason psycopg did.
sqlglot==30.17.0
